{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-par-1/order-after-delete-insert-update",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-PAR-1",
    "PAR-ORDER",
    "SQL-REL"
  ],
  "description": "R-PAR-1 PAR-ORDER, SQL-REL: How do scan order, ORDER BY k tie order and TOP 10 with ORDER BY k change on OT5 and OT3 after DELETE of every third ins, then INSERT ... SELECT of the first 20 ins rows again with ins + 1000 and pk - 500, then UPDATE k = 6 - k for every fifth ins? Reads SELECT ins, ORDER BY k and TOP 10 ORDER BY k for both tables before and after each of the three writes (one GetRows(300) per read). Runs on a fresh copy of r-par-1-order opened read-write through DAO OpenDatabase in one process and one STA; each statement is opened with Database.OpenRecordset as a snapshot unless stated, and every call's result, HRESULT and DBEngine.Errors are captured.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
